{
  "title": "Finito il lavoro, {im:camminava} parlando al telefono",
  "translation": "Once work was over, he walked along talking on the phone",
  "topics": "Participle clauses, the gerund, infinitive constructions",
  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      {
        "h": "The past participle on its own"
      },
      "A past participle can replace a whole time clause. It means *once this was done* and it's typical of written Italian. It agrees with the noun that follows, which is the thing that was completed.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Full clause",
            "Participle clause"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Dopo che il lavoro {pp:è finito}, {pp:siamo usciti}.",
              "Finit**o** il lavoro, {pp:siamo usciti}."
            ],
            [
              "Dopo che {pp:ha letto} la lettera, {pp:ha pianto}.",
              "Lett**a** la lettera, {pp:ha pianto}."
            ],
            [
              "Dopo che {tp:erano arrivati} gli ospiti, {pp:abbiamo cenato}.",
              "Arrivat**i** gli ospiti, {pp:abbiamo cenato}."
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "Pronouns attach to the participle: *Salutatolo, {pp:è uscita}* (Having said goodbye to him, she left).",
      {
        "h": "The present participle"
      },
      "It is rarely a verb in modern Italian. Mostly it has become an adjective or a noun: *interessante, divertente, importante; il cantante, l'insegnante, lo studente*.",
      {
        "h": "What the gerund can mean"
      },
      "The gerund can express time, manner, cause or concession. Its subject must be the same as that of the main verb.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Meaning",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "While",
              "{im:Camminava} parlando al telefono."
            ],
            [
              "How",
              "{pp:Ha imparato} leggendo."
            ],
            [
              "Because",
              "Avendo fame, {pp:ha mangiato}."
            ],
            [
              "Although, with pur",
              "Pur essendo stanco, {pp:ha lavorato}."
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "The compound gerund shows that the action came first: *Avendo finito, {pp:sono uscito}. Essendo partita presto, {pp:è arrivata} prima.*",
      {
        "h": "Stare + gerund and andare + gerund"
      },
      "*Stare* shows an action in progress: *{ip:Sto} leggendo*. It cannot be used with a future idea, so *{ip:Sto} partendo domani* is wrong. *Andare* + gerund shows gradual progress: *La situazione {ip:va} migliorando.*",
      {
        "h": "The infinitive in linked clauses"
      },
      "When both parts have the same subject, the infinitive is usually preferred to a full clause.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Form",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "prima di + infinitive",
              "Prima di uscire, {imv:chiudi} la porta."
            ],
            [
              "dopo aver + participle",
              "Dopo aver mangiato, {pp:siamo usciti}."
            ],
            [
              "dopo essere + participle",
              "Dopo essere arrivat**i**, {pp:abbiamo mangiato}."
            ],
            [
              "senza + infinitive",
              "{pp:È uscito} senza salutare."
            ],
            [
              "per + infinitive",
              "{ip:Studio} per superare l'esame."
            ]
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
